	(text "The BEMF circuit measures the back-electromotive force \ngenerated by the unpowered phase of the BLDC motor. The \nzero-crossing detector compares this signal with the virtual \nneutral voltage to identify zero crossings. This allows the \nrotor position to be estimated and the motor phases to be \ncommutated at the correct time without position sensors."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 125.222 102.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "31c3a34d-18cf-4d8b-ac67-50300ee39448")
	)
	(text "This half-bridge stage uses two MOSFETs and a driver to \ncontrol the switching of one phase (Phase C).\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.192 169.926 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3a864524-fc18-4d69-bb82-827c890f86f2")
	)
	(text "Power\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 136.652 229.108 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3cc8f937-c001-4319-889a-cefa620c93fc")
	)
	(text "This structure allows us to choose between the 3.3 V supply \nfrom the TIVA-C or the Buck-LDO stage. \nUsing both simultaneously could damage the circuit, \nas they are independent power sources."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 192.786 37.592 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3d0fe2e4-7d5c-45ec-a05e-92053a2325fa")
	)
